.page shift 1 drop positional parameters

# SYNOPSIS
*shift* [_N_]

# DESCRIPTION
`shift` is a gapsh builtin that removes the first _N_ (default 1) positional parameters, so that `$2` becomes `$1` and so on. It fails with status 1 if there are fewer than _N_.

# EXAMPLES
    while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do echo "arg: $1"; shift; done

# SEE ALSO
set(1), getopts(1)
